<title>UK: Air India drops ex-UK cargo fuel surcharge.</title>
<headline>Air India drops ex-UK cargo fuel surcharge.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air India dropped its ex-UK cargo fuel surcharge of six pence per kg from midnight, April 16, UK cargo manager Madhav Lokur told Reuters.</p>
<p>The surcharge was introduced last November in line with decisions taken by many other carriers concerned about rising jet fuel prices.</p>
<p>Lokur said he could not comment on the fuel surcharge policies being adopted by other Air India stations in Europe. -Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
